cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Monte Carlo uncertainty evaluation of binary-centroid pupil localisation: code and data"
abstract: >-
  Measurement model, analysis scripts and Monte Carlo results for a JCGM 101
  uncertainty evaluation of binary-centroid pupil localisation in video-oculography,
  including a closed-form coverage-fraction model of the threshold-induced bias, a
  verification on real infrared pupil geometry (LPW dataset) and the original
  MATLAB/Octave model from which the Python implementation was ported.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Ostaszewska-Liżewska
    given-names: Anna
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5203-8129"
    affiliation: "Warsaw University of Technology, Faculty of Mechatronics"
keywords:
  - measurement uncertainty
  - Monte Carlo method
  - JCGM 101
  - bias correction
  - subpixel localisation
  - eye tracking
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Labeled pupils in the wild (LPW)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bulling
        given-names: Andreas
    doi: 10.18419/DARUS-3237
    year: 2023
    notes: >-
      Third-party dataset used for the real-image verification, licensed under
      CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Not redistributed here; see README.md.
